item.text:
{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q022_colg_crya_remote_homology","answer":"SCOPe changed this pair from a fold-level resemblance to an explicit remote-homology relationship. In 2.04, the ColG collagen-binding domain d1nqda_ (SUNID 86025) was b.23.2.1: the collagen-binding family/superfamily in the CUB-like fold b.23. Cry3A domain III d1dlca1 (SUNID 23719; residues A:500–644) was b.18.1.3: the delta-endotoxin C-terminal family in the galactose-binding-domain-like fold b.18. Thus they shared only the all-beta class, and SCOPe did not then assert common ancestry. Current SCOPe is base release 2.08 (latest API update 2.08-2026-08-16). It retains Cry3A as b.18.1.3 but reclassifies ColG as b.18.1.36 (collagen-binding-domain family, SUNID 267607), placing both in fold b.18 and, critically, superfamily b.18.1 (SUNID 49785). They remain different families, so the conclusion is remote common ancestry—not close, family-level homology or interchangeable function.

The structures support that change. Both domains have the compact galactose-binding-like beta-sandwich core despite extensive sequence divergence. A direct TM-align of the API coordinates for 1nqdA against 1dlcA residues 500–644 aligned 97 residues, with 3.57 Å RMSD, 6.2% identity, and TM-scores 0.571 normalized to the 111-residue ColG domain and 0.471 normalized to the 145-residue Cry3A domain. The conserved three-dimensional core in the near-absence of detectable sequence identity is characteristic of remote homology. Independently, the stored FATCAT results for 1nqdA's 99.16%-identical cluster representative 1nqjA include the Cry4Ba C-terminal domain d1w99a3 from the same b.18.1.3 family (P=0.00395, RMSD 2.52 Å, 2.5% identity), supporting the family-level structural bridge. Those representative statistics belong to 1nqjA, however, and must not be quoted as a direct 1nqd–1dlc comparison; the direct coordinate alignment above addresses the named pair.

Function provides compatible, but weaker, support: ColG CBD3b is a noncatalytic, calcium-associated collagen-recognition module appended to a collagenase, whereas Cry3A domain III is the noncatalytic beta-sandwich recognition/specificity domain of a three-domain insecticidal toxin and participates in receptor—including glycan—interactions. Both therefore use an ancestral binding-module architecture for target recognition, followed by substantial specialization. This does not justify transferring collagen binding to Cry3A, receptor specificity or toxicity to ColG, or catalytic activity to either isolated domain. As a modeling template, either structure can guide the conserved beta-sandwich topology, but the very low identity, different lengths, and divergent surface loops preclude reliable transfer of binding-site residues, calcium dependence, ligand specificity, or full-protein function.","evidence_used":["pretrained model knowledge","/api/v1/","/api/v1/openapi.yaml","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqdA","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqdA/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1dlcA","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1dlcA/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqjA","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqjA/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sunids/89260","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sunids/89260/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49785","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49785/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49785/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Cry3A&mode=prefix&limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/4qx2A","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/4qx2A/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqdA/coordinates","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1dlcA/coordinates"]}]}
